{"title":"2019 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Bashing/Butterfly_Method)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Bashing/Butterfly Method)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(probably_won&#39;t_use_this_solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (probably won't use this solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Best_Solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Best Solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#==Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic(1_to_25_Full_Solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">==Video Solution by The Power of Logic(1 to 25 Full Solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Butterfly_Method\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Butterfly Method</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following is the correct order of the fractions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca72d717281aca63c669f5c5f278d26b708e3576.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{11},\\frac{19}{15},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"56\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/e/3be9d9b23994ac408ee01827154a6428387c2bab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{17}{13},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"26\" height=\"37\" /> from least to greatest? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/c/26cab79710133c04deb8a6ea5ed266ad4f1529bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{15}{11}&lt; \\frac{17}{13}&lt; \\frac{19}{15}  \\qquad\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{15}{11}&lt; \\frac{19}{15}&lt;\\frac{17}{13}    \\qquad\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{17}{13}&lt;\\frac{19}{15}&lt;\\frac{15}{11}    \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{19}{15}&lt;\\frac{15}{11}&lt;\\frac{17}{13}   \\qquad\\textbf{(E) }   \\frac{19}{15}&lt;\\frac{17}{13}&lt;\\frac{15}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"881\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Bashing.2FButterfly_Method.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Bashing/Butterfly_Method)\">Solution 1 (Bashing/Butterfly Method)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Bashing/Butterfly Method)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We take a common denominator:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/6/166b8126850e1a57d7eb59016ca8a9ed6c1d148c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{15}{11},\\frac{19}{15}, \\frac{17}{13} = \\frac{15\\cdot 15 \\cdot 13}{11\\cdot 15 \\cdot 13},\\frac{19 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 13}{15\\cdot 11 \\cdot 13}, \\frac{17 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 15}{13\\cdot 11 \\cdot 15} = \\frac{2925}{2145},\\frac{2717}{2145},\\frac{2805}{2145}.\\]\" width=\"540\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/2/2726b588177e92ede91145d0867ae12cb37910ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2717&lt;2805&lt;2925$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"156\" height=\"13\" /> it follows that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/f/7bf23e95cab5155dc0f79aad87fbaa882e6818d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\frac{19}{15}&lt;\\frac{17}{13}&lt;\\frac{15}{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"154\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>Another approach to this problem is using the properties of one fraction being greater than another, also known as the <b>butterfly method</b>. That is, if \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/f/35f126efdfabfd98eafb3cb19d9cdf6b11a68ab0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b}&gt;\\frac{c}{d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"53\" height=\"34\" />, then it must be true that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/9/439c2efd4e30e612327a6fedf497033130bc699c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a * d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/524e06fd69545045bfd3b8296777a12e8aed4a3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b * c$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" />. Using this approach, we can check for <b>at least</b> two distinct pairs of fractions and find out the greater one of those two, logically giving us the expected answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/f/7bf23e95cab5155dc0f79aad87fbaa882e6818d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\frac{19}{15}&lt;\\frac{17}{13}&lt;\\frac{15}{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"154\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>-xMidnightFirex\n</p><p>~ dolphin7 - I took your idea and made it an explanation.\n</p><p>- Clearness by doulai1\n</p><p>- Alternate Solution by Nivaar\n</p><p>Remark: Instead of evaluating ad and bc to see which is bigger, difference of squares is sufficient. -Supernova77\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/e/7de9d72c4230fd57c3aa9336d4f07ba9675cc1e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"46\" height=\"36\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b762d600896ea82c99d490b90c0c0d11ee4938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a6927d4492bdb8b8d88579e8ac8a6a27fa7a0454.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+z}{y+z}&lt;\\frac{x}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"86\" height=\"41\" />. Hence, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/f/7bf23e95cab5155dc0f79aad87fbaa882e6818d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\frac{19}{15}&lt;\\frac{17}{13}&lt;\\frac{15}{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"154\" height=\"48\" />.\n~ ryjs\n</p><p>This is also similar to Problem 20 on the 2012 AMC 8.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28probably_won.27t_use_this_solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(probably_won't_use_this_solution)\">Solution 3 (probably won't use this solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (probably won&#39;t use this solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We use our insane mental calculator to find out that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/b/7ebcca60b61f31b7d5801242886c4b784971d259.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{11} \\approx 1.36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/82070118518da24af323599bd2591d2552aa7641.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{19}{15} \\approx 1.27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/1/5110b2dfb500bab8c6b2a1942a3e7d097cdf6b5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{17}{13} \\approx 1.31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/f/7bf23e95cab5155dc0f79aad87fbaa882e6818d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\frac{19}{15}&lt;\\frac{17}{13}&lt;\\frac{15}{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"154\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>~~ by an insane math guy.\n~~ random text that is here to distract you.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose each fraction is expressed with denominator <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a4abf524df5ee5ff3096778c57f64f144517b93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2145$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/a/36a29eab9e545cffcbe327799b670e9d3cbdac1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2925}{2145}, \\frac{2717}{2145}, \\frac{2805}{2145}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"135\" height=\"38\" />. Clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/2/2726b588177e92ede91145d0867ae12cb37910ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2717&lt;2805&lt;2925$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"156\" height=\"13\" /> so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bfc0829f3f29bbf35d0a861644e00cfef0f50ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Note: Duplicate of Solution 1</li></ul>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Best_Solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Best_Solution)\">Solution 5 (Best Solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Best Solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We notice that each of these fractions' numerator <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add22d9bda21e86390bc74fa4dde17730a442da7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> denominator <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80b89184403920af48463d99f172dc31508732dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />. If we take each of the fractions, and subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> from each, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/f/35f5c84df68a1ad89a14d0ee87c5c32a7855b245.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/0386f0700801b41f9f5b63f1ac94adb2ad23c881.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/e/73ee333c86c86590cef0a7101ac38a9d6789ec1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />. These are easy to order because the numerators are the same, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/0/4a0a8cd10a921460e321cc3473039aba12fd2391.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{15}&lt;\\frac{4}{13}&lt;\\frac{4}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"113\" height=\"37\" />. Because it is a subtraction by a constant, to order them, we keep the inequality signs to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/a/4fad15016d1502619128196d3fe75c9534e2b4d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\;\\frac{19}{15}&lt;\\frac{17}{13}&lt;\\frac{15}{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"159\" height=\"48\" />.\n--SweetMango77\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Adding on to Solution 5, we can turn each of the fractions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/b/b4b11b1bf8ccfbb5b74fe3dd9f360bf30c7ebd0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/1/d01e469c0241f2d6c5537ca4817550311d2854e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{17}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/1/f716304060cc3e1e08617ea6326a3d063d1551b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{19}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/f/35f5c84df68a1ad89a14d0ee87c5c32a7855b245.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/e/73ee333c86c86590cef0a7101ac38a9d6789ec1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/0386f0700801b41f9f5b63f1ac94adb2ad23c881.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, respectively. We now subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> from each to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/f/35f5c84df68a1ad89a14d0ee87c5c32a7855b245.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/0386f0700801b41f9f5b63f1ac94adb2ad23c881.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/e/73ee333c86c86590cef0a7101ac38a9d6789ec1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />. Since their numerators are all 4, this is easy because we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/e/cfeb86eadb2f6d7f0fa16dcdffbdbbe2abce0c27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{15}&lt;\\frac{1}{13}&lt;\\frac{1}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"117\" height=\"38\" /> and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/0/4a0a8cd10a921460e321cc3473039aba12fd2391.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{15}&lt;\\frac{4}{13}&lt;\\frac{4}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"113\" height=\"37\" />. Reverting them to their original fractions, we can now see that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/a/4fad15016d1502619128196d3fe75c9534e2b4d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\;\\frac{19}{15}&lt;\\frac{17}{13}&lt;\\frac{15}{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"159\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>~by ChipmunkT\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As you can see that the difference between the numerator and denominator is 4, you can guess the relative ratios and you can scale down and make it <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/3/373c38eba8ae931c67a3861d58b82d71a8044dc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{5},\\frac{7}{3},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"41\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/addc48074e8ae42835ec24a202159bee72bfb4b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{1},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" />. Using this, you can very clearly tell that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/addc48074e8ae42835ec24a202159bee72bfb4b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{1},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> is the greatest and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/b/b4b11b1bf8ccfbb5b74fe3dd9f360bf30c7ebd0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" />, is the greatest. You can use the same method to find the other 2 orders. This gives the answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/a/4fad15016d1502619128196d3fe75c9534e2b4d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\;\\frac{19}{15}&lt;\\frac{17}{13}&lt;\\frac{15}{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"159\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>Note-this answer only works in some circumstances, and overall solution 6 is much better.\n</p><p>~ParticlePhysics\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_.28First_fully_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IgpayYB48C4?si=-TpVe8QyZbbc6yKr&amp;t=266\">https://youtu.be/IgpayYB48C4?si=-TpVe8QyZbbc6yKr&amp;t=266</a>\n</p><p>~Math-X\n</p><p>The Learning Royal: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IiFFDDITE6Q\">https://youtu.be/IiFFDDITE6Q</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Solution detailing how to solve the problem: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q27qEcr7TbQ&amp;list=PLbhMrFqoXXwmwbk2CWeYOYPRbGtmdPUhL&amp;index=4\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q27qEcr7TbQ&amp;list=PLbhMrFqoXXwmwbk2CWeYOYPRbGtmdPUhL&amp;index=4</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3\">Video Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/xNrhMAbaEcI\">https://youtu.be/xNrhMAbaEcI</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zI2f4GpQPIo\">https://youtu.be/zI2f4GpQPIo</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\".3D.3DVideo_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic.281_to_25_Full_Solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"==Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic(1_to_25_Full_Solution)\">==Video Solution by The Power of Logic(1 to 25 Full Solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: ==Video Solution by The Power of Logic(1 to 25 Full Solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Xm4ZGND9WoY\">https://youtu.be/Xm4ZGND9WoY</a>\n</p><p>~Hayabusa1\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Butterfly_Method\">Butterfly Method</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Butterfly Method\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The butterfly method is a method where you multiply the denominator of the second fraction and multiply it by the numerator from the first fraction.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8\" title=\"2019 AMC 8\">2019 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2019 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2019 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2019\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2019 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2019 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2019 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2019 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2019 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2019 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2019 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a